-- title:
--   Covolume rates of GL₂(A_K) and a twisted centraliser
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq L$ be number fields with $[L:K] = 2$ (`h2`), let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$ (`hgen`), let $\delta_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, let $c$ be a unit of $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K$ and $u$ a unit of $\mathbb{A}_K$, where $\mathbb{A}_K$ denotes the adele ring of $K$. Throughout, $\delta$ denotes the element $\bigl(\delta_0 \otimes 1\bigr)\cdot (c\,I) \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$, that is the image of $\delta_0$ under the entrywise map induced by $\ell \mapsto \ell \otimes 1$ times the scalar matrix of $c$; $\sigma$ acts on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K A)$ for any $K$-algebra $A$ entrywise through $\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id}_A$, and for $\delta' \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K A)$ the *twisted centraliser* of $\delta'$ is the subgroup $\{t \mid t\,\delta'\,\sigma(t)^{-1} = \delta'\}$. The archimedean and $v$-adic components of $\delta$ are its images under the entrywise maps induced by $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K \to L \otimes_K K_\infty$ and $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K \to L \otimes_K K_v$, written `tensorArch` and `tensorPlace`. All general linear groups over topological rings, and the centralisers and twisted centralisers occurring below, carry their Borel $\sigma$-algebras.
--
--   The hypotheses are as follows.
--
--   *Norm-string condition* `hN`: the product $\delta \cdot \sigma(\delta)$ (the product of $(\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}})^{i}(\delta)$ for $i$ running over $\{0,\dots,[L:K]-1\}$) equals the image of the scalar matrix $u\,I \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ under the entrywise map induced by $a \mapsto 1 \otimes a$.
--
--   *Ellipticity* `hns`: for every $x \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ and every $z \in L^\times$, $x^{-1}\,\delta_0\,\sigma(x) \neq z\,I$; that is, $\delta_0$ is not $\sigma$-conjugate over $L$ to a scalar matrix.
--
--   *Local measures* `hτa`, `hτa'`, `hτf`, `hτf'`: $\tau_a$ is a Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_\infty)$, $\tau_a'$ a Haar measure on the twisted centraliser of the archimedean component of $\delta$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_\infty)$, and for each finite place $v$ of $K$ (a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$) $\tau_{f,v}$ is a Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ and $\tau_{f,v}'$ a Haar measure on the twisted centraliser of the $v$-component of $\delta$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$.
--
--   *Archimedean matching* `harch`: with $K_\infty$ made an $\mathbb{R}$-algebra through the identification with the mixed space of $K$ and $L \otimes_K K_\infty$ an $\mathbb{R}$-algebra through $a \mapsto 1 \otimes a$, there exist natural numbers $n_1, n_2$, families $e_1 : \mathrm{Fin}\,n_1 \to M_2(L \otimes_K K_\infty)$ and $e_2 : \mathrm{Fin}\,n_2 \to M_2(L \otimes_K K_\infty)$, and $s \in [0,\infty]$ with $s \neq 0$ and $s \neq \infty$, such that: $e_1$ is $\mathbb{R}$-linearly independent and its $\mathbb{R}$-span is the image of $M_2(K_\infty)$ under the entrywise map induced by $a \mapsto 1 \otimes a$; $e_2$ is $\mathbb{R}$-linearly independent and its $\mathbb{R}$-span is $\{X \mid X\,\delta_\infty = \delta_\infty\,\sigma(X)\}$, where $\delta_\infty$ is the archimedean component of $\delta$ and $\sigma$ acts entrywise; the pushforward of $\tau_a$ under $t \mapsto$ (the matrix of $t$, mapped entrywise by $a \mapsto 1 \otimes a$) equals $s$ times the measure obtained from Lebesgue measure on $\mathbb{R}^{n_1}$ transported by $c \mapsto \sum_i c_i e_1(i)$, scaled by $\sqrt{\lvert \det (\mathrm{tr}_{\mathbb{R}}(\mathrm{tr}(e_1(i)e_1(j))))_{i,j}\rvert}$ and given the density $X \mapsto \lvert N_{\mathbb{R}}(\det X)\rvert^{-1}$; and the pushforward of $\tau_a'$ under the inclusion of the twisted centraliser into $M_2(L \otimes_K K_\infty)$ equals the corresponding expression formed with the same $s$, with $e_2$ and its Gram determinant in place of $e_1$, and with the same density $X \mapsto \lvert N_{\mathbb{R}}(\det X)\rvert^{-1}$. Here $\mathrm{tr}_{\mathbb{R}}$ and $N_{\mathbb{R}}$ are the trace and norm of the $\mathbb{R}$-algebra $L \otimes_K K_\infty$ and $\mathrm{tr}$ is the matrix trace.
--
--   *Matching at the finite places* `hfin`: for every finite place $v$, one of the following two alternatives holds. Either there is $y \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ which is a norm conjugator in the sense that the image of the $v$-component of the scalar matrix $u\,I$ under $a \mapsto 1 \otimes a$ equals $y^{-1}\bigl(\delta_v \sigma(\delta_v)\bigr) y$, where $\delta_v$ is the $v$-component of $\delta$, and moreover the pushforward of $\tau_{f,v}'$ under $t \mapsto y^{-1} t y$ equals the pushforward of $\tau_{f,v}$ under the entrywise map $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ induced by $a \mapsto 1 \otimes a$. Or else both of the following hold: for no unit $z$ of $L \otimes_K K_v$ is $z\,I$ of the form $x^{-1}\delta_v \sigma(x)$ with $x \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$; and, writing $T_v^{1}$ for the set of $t$ in the twisted centraliser of $\delta_v$ whose determinant is the image under $a \mapsto 1 \otimes a$ of some unit $s$ of $K_v$ with $\lvert s\rvert_v = 1$, one has
--   $$\tau_{f,v}'(T_v^{1}) \cdot \lvert \mathcal{O}_K/v\rvert = \tau_{f,v}\bigl(\{g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v) \mid g \text{ and } g^{-1} \text{ have entries in } \mathcal{O}_{K_v}\}\bigr) + \tau_{f,v}'(T_v^{1}),$$
--   the factor being the absolute norm of the ideal $v$ read in $[0,\infty]$.
--
--   *Restricted-product factorisations* `hτprod` and `hτ'prod`, relative to a finite set $S_0$ of finite places: $\tau$ is a Haar measure on the centraliser of the scalar matrix $u\,I$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, $c_\tau > 0$, and for every finite set $S \supseteq S_0$ of finite places and all functions $W$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, $W_a$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_\infty)$ and $W_{S,v}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ such that $W_a$ is almost everywhere strongly measurable for $\tau_a$, each $W_{S,v}$ with $v \in S$ is almost everywhere strongly measurable for $\tau_{f,v}$, $W(t) = W_a(t_\infty)\prod_{v \in S} W_{S,v}(t_v)$ for every $t$ in the centraliser all of whose components outside $S$ lie in the set of $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ with $g$ and $g^{-1}$ integral, and $W(t) = 0$ for every $t$ in the centraliser having some component outside $S$ not of that form, one has $\int W \,\mathrm{d}\tau = c_\tau \bigl(\int W_a \,\mathrm{d}\tau_a\bigr)\prod_{v \in S}\int W_{S,v}\,\mathrm{d}\tau_{f,v}$. Symmetrically, $\tau'$ is a Haar measure on the twisted centraliser of $\delta$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$, $c_{\tau'} > 0$, and the same factorisation statement holds with $\tau_a'$, $\tau_{f,v}'$, the archimedean and $v$-adic component maps `tensorArch`, `tensorPlace`, and with the local integrality condition replaced by membership in the set of $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ such that $g$ and $g^{-1}$ have entries in the image of the semilocal integers, yielding $\int W \,\mathrm{d}\tau' = c_{\tau'}\bigl(\int W_a\,\mathrm{d}\tau_a'\bigr)\prod_{v \in S}\int W_{S,v}\,\mathrm{d}\tau_{f,v}'$.
--
--   *Logarithmic rates* `hD`, `hD'`, with constants $R, R' \in [0,\infty]$, both finite (`hR`, `hR'`): for every subset $D$ of the centraliser of $u\,I$ which is a fundamental domain, with respect to $\tau$, for the right translation action of the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ in that centraliser, and for all reals $0 < a \le b$,
--   $$\tau\bigl(D \cap \{t \mid \lVert \det t\rVert_K \in [a,b]\}\bigr) = R\,\log(b/a),$$
--   where $\lVert\cdot\rVert_K$ is the idele norm, given by the distributive Haar character of $\mathbb{A}_K$; and for every subset $D'$ of the twisted centraliser of $\delta$ which is a fundamental domain, with respect to $\tau'$, for the right translation action of the image of $\{t \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L) \mid t\,\delta_0\,\sigma(t)^{-1} = \delta_0\}$ under the entrywise map induced by $\ell \mapsto \ell \otimes 1$, and for all reals $0 < a \le b$,
--   $$\tau'\bigl(D' \cap \{t \mid \lVert \det \tilde{t}\rVert_L \in [a,b]\}\bigr) = R'\,\log(b/a),$$
--   where $\tilde{t} \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ is the image of $t$ under the entrywise map induced by the ring isomorphism $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K \cong \mathbb{A}_K \otimes_K L \cong \mathbb{A}_L$ (the commutation isomorphism followed by `genuineRingEquiv`).
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is the single identity
--   $$c_{\tau'} \cdot R = 2\,c_\tau \cdot R'$$
--   in $[0,\infty]$, with $c_\tau$ and $c_{\tau'}$ read as elements of $[0,\infty]$.
--
--   This is the comparison of global covolume rates entering the Jacquet–Langlands matching of orbital integrals: the rate per unit of $\log$ of the idele norm of the determinant for $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over $K$ against that for the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser of an elliptic $\delta_0$, the factor $2$ reflecting $\lVert\cdot\rVert_L = \lVert\cdot\rVert_K^{2}$ on norms from the quadratic extension. It is used by [`AutomorphicForm.mul_eq_mul_of_isTwistedOrbitalIntegralOn_of_isOrbitalIntegralOn_centralScalar_of_forall_ne_scalar_of_finrank_eq_two`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.mul_eq_mul_of_isTwistedOrbitalIntegralOn_of_isOrbitalIntegralOn_centralScalar_of_forall_ne_scalar_of_finrank_eq_two), where the orbital integral at a central class is compared with the corresponding twisted orbital integral.
